@page "/privacy"
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How ShizuStore handles data in the website and the Android app.";
}

<article class="privacy">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>
        ShizuStore is an open-source app store for Shizuku apps. This page describes what
        data the website at shizustore.com and the ShizuStore Android app process.
    </p>

    <h2>Website</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>The website has no user accounts, cookies, or analytics scripts.</li>
        <li>
            Like any web server, the API and storefront log requests (timestamp, IP address,
            requested path and User-Agent) to protect the service from abuse and to produce
            aggregate usage statistics. Logs are not used to identify individuals.
        </li>
        <li>
            The site is served through Cloudflare, which proxies requests and may process
            your IP address and User-Agent for security and performance purposes under
            its own
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
            Pages may show images from upstream project pages or GitHub; those requests are
            governed by the respective site's privacy policy.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Android app</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>The app has no user accounts and does not collect personal data.</li>
        <li>
            When you install an app, the app sends an anonymous install report to the API
            containing the app's slug, version code and whether it was a fresh install or an
            update. No device or user identifiers are attached.
        </li>
        <li>
            Catalog requests contain no account or device identifiers; the server records
            aggregate request and User-Agent statistics.
        </li>
        <li>
            APK downloads go directly from your device to the upstream project page.
            ShizuStore never mirrors APKs.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
        Questions go to
        <a href="mailto:shizustore@timschneeberger.me">shizustore@timschneeberger.me</a>
        or via the
        <a href="https://github.com/timschneeb/ShizuStore/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub issue tracker</a>.
    </p>
</article>
